@startuml fig-12-participant-state-machine
' =====================================================================
' Figure 12. Your status in the study, and every way it can legally change
' Type            : PlantUML-type, state machine with guarded transitions
' Paper section   : § 5, Study Design Explained
' Concern answered: ChatGPT concern 7 (unknown and experimental risks) and
'                   concern 8 (randomization and treatment choice). A patient
'                   who is told the study is "open-label, single-arm, 3+3" has
'                   been given three technical terms and no information. A
'                   guarded state machine says the same thing operationally:
'                   there is one arm, so no allocation can go against you; the
'                   dose level you receive is determined by what happened to
'                   the people before you; and every transition has a named
'                   guard that must evaluate true.
' Why this type   : Guards are the point. A Mermaid state diagram shows the
'                   states; PlantUML notation shows the guard condition on each
'                   transition, which is where the protection actually lives.
'
' TikZ: draw with the uml* vocabulary of patientstyle.sty.
' TikZ: umlinit filled disc at (0,1.6); umlfinal ringed disc at (0,-15.4).
' TikZ: umlstate rounded boxes, text width 34mm, single column at x = 0,
' TikZ:   y = 0, -2.4, -4.8, -7.2, -9.6, -12.0, -14.0; 2.4 cm pitch leaves
' TikZ:   at least 9 mm of clear space between ranks.
' TikZ: The two off-path states, Cohort hold and Not enrolled, sit at
' TikZ:   x = 6.8 and x = -6.8 respectively, vertically aligned with the state
' TikZ:   they branch from, so no transition crosses the main column.
' TikZ: Guards are set in a white-filled mmlabel node at the transition
' TikZ:   midpoint, in \tiny\sffamily, bracketed, never on the line.
' TikZ: Return transitions from Cohort hold use
' TikZ:   to[out=180,in=0,looseness=0.9]; the self-transition on Dose assigned
' TikZ:   uses to[out=35,in=-35,looseness=5] on a 5 mm right-hand loop.
' TikZ: umlstateon (Corporate Blue fill) marks the two states in which the
' TikZ:   participant is receiving the investigational intervention.
' =====================================================================

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #6C757D
skinparam ArrowFontColor #111111
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam StateBorderColor #00417A
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam StateFontColor #111111
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E9ECEF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #6C757D

[*] --> Screened

state Screened #FFFFFF : Screening, day -28 to -1\nKRAS G12 confirmed, staging done
state "Not enrolled" as NotEnr #E9ECEF : Screen failure or declined\nMinimal data set only, § 5.4\nStandard care unchanged
state Enrolled #DCE8F1 : Consent on file\nSoftware version frozen and recorded
state "Cohort hold" as Hold #CED4DA : Sentinel window open\nNo further participant dosed\nuntil the window closes
state DoseAssigned #DCE8F1 : Dose level assigned\nDL1, DL2, or DL3 by 3+3 rule\nNever above a level not yet cleared
state Operative #00417A : Day 0, robotic Whipple\nContinuous human oversight
state Recovering #00417A : Days 1 to 30\nDaraxonrasib restart advisory
state Confirmed #DCE8F1 : Day 90\nR0 pathology, 90-day mortality
state LongTerm #FFFFFF : Every 12 weeks to 24 months\nPFS and OS

Screened --> NotEnr : [ineligible OR declined]
Screened --> Enrolled : [all § 5.1 met]\n[no § 5.2 exclusion]\n[consent signed]
Enrolled --> Hold : [prior participant\nstill inside the\nsentinel window]
Hold --> DoseAssigned : [sentinel window closed]\n[no DLT declared]
Enrolled --> DoseAssigned : [no sentinel window open]
DoseAssigned --> DoseAssigned : [DLT observed in cohort]\n/ expand 3 to 6, do not escalate
DoseAssigned --> Operative : [Phase 0 gate signed]\n[USL >= 7.0 verified]\n[pre-procedure matrix clear]
Operative --> Recovering : [procedure complete\nOR converted to open]
Recovering --> Confirmed : [day-30 window closed]
Confirmed --> LongTerm : [day-90 assessments done]
LongTerm --> [*] : [24-month endpoint\nOR withdrawal\nOR death]

NotEnr --> [*]

note right of Hold
  This state exists so that you are never
  the second person at a new dose level
  before the first person's safety window
  has closed. It costs the study time.
  It is not there for the study's benefit.
end note

note left of DoseAssigned
  Single arm, open label. There is no
  allocation that could assign you to a
  comparator, and nothing about your
  treatment is concealed from you.
end note

note bottom of Operative
  Conversion to open surgery is a normal
  outcome of this state, not a failure of it.
  It is recorded, reported, and does not end
  your participation.
end note

@enduml
